{"name":"Eagles Nest","hex":"#8a693f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eagles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of eagle"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of eagle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eagles"},{"term":"nest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A structure built by a bird as a place to incubate eggs and rear young.","Any of various similar structures or sites used by other animals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build or settle into a nest.","To settle into a home."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eagle's Nest Park","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle's Nest Park is a scenic lookout in the town of Bancroft, Ontario, Canada. It is built on the top of a sheer rock face and overlooks the northern portions of the town, the York River and Bancroft Airport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Viewing_platform_in_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg/330px-Viewing_platform_in_Eagle%27s_Nest_Park-Bancroft-Ontario-20210901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle's_Nest_Park"},{"title":"Eagles Nest (Colorado)","blocks":[{"text":"Eagles Nest is a 13,419-foot (4,090 m) mountain summit in Summit County, Colorado, United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Eagles_Nest%2C_Colorado.jpg/330px-Eagles_Nest%2C_Colorado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagles_Nest_(Colorado)"},{"title":"Eagle","blocks":[{"text":"Eagle is the common name for certain large predatory birds of prey within the family of the Accipitridae. While on a genetic level, only the subfamily Aquilinae comprises \"true eagles\", many other species are commonly referred to as eagles, such as the bald eagle, and the